Airsoft Team Tracker
A wearable GPS + LoRa tracker that shows direction and distance of teammates without cell service or internet requirment. Built for airsoft but can have other applications.

Status: rough working prototype


Each player wears a node. Every node:

    Gets its position from a GNSS receiver
    Broadcasts that position to teammates over LoRa (peer-to-peer, adding mesh in later iteration)
    Receives teammates' positions and calculates distance and bearing
    Shows information on dispay

packets are encrypted using AES-128-CTR so different teams and squads do not read each others location.

as of right now you can pair watches and be in same team by creating a secrets.h in the include folder and adding a  16-byte AES-128 key shared by all devices on your team.
    #pragma once
   // 16-byte AES-128 key shared by all devices on your team
   static const uint8_t TEAM_KEY[16] = { /* your 16 bytes here */ };

Hardware
    Heltec Wireless Tracker V1.1
    915 MHz LoRa antennas
    Active ceramic GPS patch antenna
    3.7V 320mAh LiPo
    GY-BNO055 9-axis IMU


Software
    C++ on Arduino framework
    Built with PlatformIO in VS Code
    LoRa radio, GNSS parsing, display driver, and AES-128-CTR encryption


Challanges so far:
    Heading:
        deciding how the device should decide heading with multiple options and all having pros and cons 
            1. Deciding a certian side of the watch is forward
            2. North is always forward
            3. Forward is decided by tracking movement using GPS locations
    Compass module:
        got a module without built in accelerometer and gyroscope making is too innacurate for use
    Pairing:
        easier way to pair the devices with teammates on feild instead of accessing the code 

Working:
    Two-board LoRa transmit and receive
    GPS fix and position parsing
    Display output
    Direction calculation between nodes
    AES-128-CTR encrypt/decrypt round trip


In progress 
    BNO055 IMU integration for orientation (had to be redone)
    Status button to share status with teammates
    Deep-sleep soft-off with button wake (prototype); soft-latch power circuit for the final build
    Water proof Enclosure and wrist mounting 
    Mesh system to increase range 
    Possible compatiblity addition to ITAK/ATAK
    

This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
